ORIGIN / THROUGH-LINE (Peter 2026-08-10) — the whole strand answers ONE original problem: MANUAL WINDOW-PLACEMENT CHAOS. forkterm/strandterm spawned each strand as its own terminal-emulator WINDOW → you hunted for them in the taskbar, a scatter you had to hand-arrange and re-find (worsened by backend-clobbers-net-wm-name: windows wouldn't stay identifiable OR raisable — see that memory). THE ARC: (1) forkterm/strandterm = strands as separate OS windows = the disease (scatter). (2) tmux deck = put them ALL on ONE surface so the WM can't scatter them — cured the scatter, but tmux is a rigid compositor so it brought jumps + can't-share-with-browser (prototype). (3) browser compositor (downward-scroll main area + right thumbnail strip + driver agent) = the real cure: one surface, no scatter, no jump, AND can hold a browser — because YOU own the compositor (CSS), not the WM, not tmux. THROUGH-LINE: never let the window manager place things; each step takes compositing away from the OS/WM into a surface you control, tmux→browser being 'somewhere expressive enough to be pleasant'. The THUMBNAIL STRIP is the direct answer to 'hunting in the taskbar' — the taskbar was the FAILED navigator, the strip is the working one. Anchors the product model [20260810T082947Z-cziQvD] to the problem it solves.
